INT. KARAOKE BAR BACK OFFICE - NIGHT

Muffled singing through the wall. A desk, a safe, a stained couch.

VITO ARCARO, fifties, sits behind the desk. Rings. Calm.

DMITRI SOKOLOV, forties, stands by the safe. Arms crossed.

MERCEDES OYELADE, thirties, the new accountant, sits on the couch. Laptop open.

"SPOONS" FINNEGAN, twenties, holds the door. Mostly.

VITO
Count it again.

MERCEDES
I counted twice. It's short by nine thousand.

DMITRI
He took it.

VITO
Who?

DMITRI
Spoons.

SPOONS
I didn't take nothing.

DMITRI
He took it. He's got the key.

VITO
Dmitri, he took it, you say. He says he didn't. Mercedes says it's short.

MERCEDES
I say it's short. I don't say who.

SPOONS
Boss, I swear --

VITO
(softly)
Sit.

Spoons sits. Dmitri doesn't. Through the wall, someone hits a very sharp note on "My Way."

VITO (CONT'D)
Dmitri. You've been here eleven years. Why would he steal from you?

DMITRI
He wouldn't. I would.

Silence. Vito smiles. Mercedes closes the laptop.
